00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:17.860
The United States is reviewing its troop deployments across Europe,

00:00:18.220 --> 00:00:21.920
tying future commitments to weather allies, meet defense spending targets,

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:24.660
and shifting long-term security responsibilities.

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:30.600
U.S. Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth stated that a review of American forces in Europe

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:34.420
will assess whether allies are meeting defense spending goals.

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:39.900
The process is described as more than routine with contributions potentially reduced

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:46.160
for countries that fall short. Officials indicated the goal is to move NATO toward Europe taking

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:52.780
primary responsibility for its own defense. U.S. officials emphasize that the review will reward

00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:56.940
countries meeting targets while adjusting support for those that do not.

00:00:57.760 --> 00:01:02.240
European governments have described current spending trends as moving in the right direction,

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:05.000
but requiring more time to reach full alignment.

00:01:05.780 --> 00:01:09.860
Treasury and defense planners in Washington argue that conditioning U.S.

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:15.560
dues on verified spending creates direct incentives for allies to increase budgets.

00:01:16.360 --> 00:01:21.980
European NATO members counter that abrupt adjustments risk weakening the integrated command structure

00:01:21.980 --> 00:01:28.340
built over decades. What specific spending data will determine whether a country passes or fails

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:34.520
the review? Shifting now to events in Poland, authorities in Lublin detained a suspect in

00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:41.180
the shooting death of Russian artist Semyon Skrepewski. Prime Minister Donald Tusk confirmed the

00:01:41.180 --> 00:01:46.180
arrest while noting investigators continue to search for anyone who may have directed the attack.

00:01:47.020 --> 00:01:51.160
Polish officials have framed the case as a straightforward criminal investigation

00:01:51.160 --> 00:01:57.440
with no immediate political attribution. Russian opposition voices have pointed to the victim's

00:01:57.440 --> 00:02:03.140
public criticism of the Kremlin as a likely motive. Polish investigators stress that evidence

00:02:03.140 --> 00:02:08.940
collection remains the priority and that any mastermind will be pursued through standard legal channels.

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:16.060
Russian dissident networks argue that the timing and target selection fit a documented history

00:02:16.060 --> 00:02:21.400
