00:07:42.720 --> 00:07:49.020
Now, to really understand the NATO spending debate, there is a mechanism most coverage leaves out.

00:07:49.500 --> 00:07:55.680
The 2% target originated as a political benchmark rather than a legally binding treaty obligation.

00:07:56.400 --> 00:08:00.780
This allows each ally to interpret compliance through its own budget process

00:08:00.780 --> 00:08:06.340
and definitions of defense spending. When the United States links future troop levels or

00:08:06.340 --> 00:08:12.300
basing decisions to verified spending, it converts that non-binding goal into a practical

00:08:12.300 --> 00:08:17.040
lever that affects integrated command structures and joint procurement programs.

00:08:17.640 --> 00:08:21.580
Next time you hear claims that Europe is not paying its fair share,

00:08:21.580 --> 00:08:27.800
ask whether the statement refers to the formal target actual outlays on deployable capabilities

00:08:27.800 --> 00:08:34.380
